Error case: on 2026-11-01 the clocks in New York go back at 02:00 EDT, so 01:30 happens twice (05:30 and 06:30 UTC). The list holds a nap at each, so a match could delete the wrong one. The time is refused before the prompt, no write is sent and the exit code is 1.
-- args --
health
sleep
naps
delete
2026-11-01
01:30
-- route GET /userprofile-service/userprofile/settings --
{"displayName":"tester","timeZone":"America/New_York"}
-- route GET /sleep-service/sleep/naps/2026-11-01 --
[{"napStartTimestampGMT":"2026-11-01T05:30:00","napTimeSec":600},{"napStartTimestampGMT":"2026-11-01T06:30:00","napTimeSec":600}]
-- table stdout --
-- table stderr --
the time 01:30 is ambiguous on 2026-11-01 in your Garmin time zone (America/New_York) because the clocks go back
-- table exit --
1
-- table requests --
GET /userprofile-service/userprofile/settings
GET /sleep-service/sleep/naps/2026-11-01
